      check('F ~ kappa (NONANALYTIC |k0|/a0) at small kappa')
  kappa = k0/a0 is a REAL Euclidean frequency, so the kernel's argument is kappa^2 >= 0.
  The negative-z region -- and a fortiori z < -1 -- is NEVER sampled by the boundedness step.

         kappa   F_1 = K_1(kappa^2)   F_2 = K_2(kappa^2)
